WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 0.1 · Start Here: Your Founder Journey
How this course works

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Decide in the order founders need to: each course builds on the one before.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
This course is a path through the decisions a founder makes, in the order they are usually needed. Each step builds on the one before, so you lay foundations instead of repairing them later.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Four courses, one order

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:40.833
Clarify: Why should this exist, and what change will you pursue? Modules 00 to 02. For example: Our bakery writes its purpose and the change it wants before choosing a legal form.

6
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:54.756
Organise: Who will decide, who will do the work and how it will run day to day. Modules 03 to 05. For example: The two co-founders agree who approves spending and how new trainees are welcomed.

7
00:00:54.756 --> 00:01:07.196
Prove & Show: How you will know it works, and how you will show it. Modules 06 to 08. For example: Our bakery picks three signs of progress, a name and a simple logo.

8
00:01:07.196 --> 00:01:21.207
Protect: How you will stay solvent, legal and safe from the start. Modules 09 and 10. For example: Our bakery drafts a first-year budget and a safeguarding policy before the first trainee starts.

9
00:01:21.607 --> 00:01:22.207
Why the order matters

10
00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:28.622
1. Most early questions depend on what you are for and who you serve.

11
00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:34.296
2. Deciding in order saves rebuilding your registration, budget or brand later.

12
00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:40.970
3. You can see what to do now and what can wait.

13
00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:41.970
How each lesson works

14
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.904
1. A short video, a written explanation and an exercise.

15
00:01:46.904 --> 00:01:52.207
2. Your answers save into your founding pack as you go.

16
00:01:52.207 --> 00:01:59.622
3. Download each module as a PDF to share with a co-founder or adviser.

17
00:02:00.022 --> 00:02:00.622
What to avoid

18
00:02:00.622 --> 00:02:06.296
Jumping to registration or money before knowing what you are for.

19
00:02:06.296 --> 00:02:10.489
Trying to finish everything in one sitting.

20
00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:17.904
Treating a first draft as final: mark what is uncertain and come back.

21
00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.304
You write your priority module, what it depends on and when you will reach it.

22
00:02:20.304 --> 00:02:24.304
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:25.804 --> 00:02:28.904
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
